{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.GroupoidTerminalDichotomy","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.GroupoidTerminalDichotomy","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Groupoid","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Limits.Shapes.Terminal"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.terminal_dichotomy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.terminal_dichotomy","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GroupoidTerminalDichotomy.lean#L88-L98","doc":"The dichotomy in one statement: in a groupoid, either no object is terminal,\nor every object is.  There is no middle case in which terminality picks out a\ncanonical object. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.isEmpty_isTerminal_of_ne_id","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.isEmpty_isTerminal_of_ne_id","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GroupoidTerminalDichotomy.lean#L79-L86","doc":"**Second horn.**  A single non-identity endomorphism anywhere in a groupoid\nrules out a terminal object everywhere.  This is the horn that applies to\nPenner's Ptolemy groupoid, whose automorphism groups are mapping-class groups,\nand to a Pachner groupoid on symmetry-orbits of triangulations of a manifold\nwith non-trivial symmetry group. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.endo_eq_id_of_isTerminal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.endo_eq_id_of_isTerminal","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GroupoidTerminalDichotomy.lean#L74-L77","doc":"In a groupoid with a terminal object, every endomorphism is the identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.isTerminal_of_isTerminal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.isTerminal_of_isTerminal","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GroupoidTerminalDichotomy.lean#L64-L72","doc":"**First horn.**  In a groupoid, one terminal object makes every object\nterminal.  Terminality therefore distinguishes no decomposition from any\nother. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.homOfIsTerminal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.homOfIsTerminal","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GroupoidTerminalDichotomy.lean#L58-L62","doc":"In a groupoid with a terminal object, every hom-set is inhabited: compose\ninto `T` and back out again.  Together with\n`hom_subsingleton_of_isTerminal` this makes every hom-set a singleton. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.hom_subsingleton_of_isTerminal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.hom_subsingleton_of_isTerminal","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GroupoidTerminalDichotomy.lean#L52-L56","doc":"In a groupoid, a terminal object collapses *every* hom-set to at most one\nmorphism.  Right-cancel the invertible `hT.from Y`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}